{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And I will put it in the hand of those who afflict you.</b> From the root of יגון, and it is in the heavy [passive] stem [binyan] like אשה הוגה (Lamentations 1:12)." "<b>Bow down.</b> And be humbled, and let us pass over you." "<b>And like dirt.</b> The meaning is doubled [i.e., a hendiadys]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:06.426033331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}